# The demo image's Caddy configuration template (Lane 0 sub item 1): multi-app
# shape. The entrypoint substitutes the placeholders and pipes the result to
# Caddy on standard input; Caddy's autosave of the adapted configuration is
# pointed at the container's shared-memory tmpfs, so nothing generated and no
# secret reaches the image's layers, a volume, or anything that outlives the
# container.
#
# Placeholders:
#   __GATE_PORT__  the public port Caddy listens on (the platform's PORT)
#   __UPSTREAM__   the core's loopback address and port
#   __GATE_HASH__  the shared phrase's bcrypt hash, from the runtime value
#                  the operator sets; substituted by the entrypoint at
#                  boot, never baked into the image
#
# The gate (G6): basic authentication on the pages and on the demo mint
# routes, and on nothing else. Every other api route is the core's own
# law, which is why a staff call with a valid demo bearer and no phrase
# still answers, and /healthz answers unauthenticated for the platform.
#
# The handle blocks are ordered most specific first: the demo mint routes,
# then every other api route, then the health leg, then each app's prefixed
# static route, and finally everything else which is the front door.
#
# Each app is served under its own prefix with its own file root. The base
# path each app builds with (Vite's base option) is encoded in its asset
# references, and handle_path strips the prefix before the file server looks
# the file up in the app's own root, so the assets resolve correctly.
#
# The forwarded address discipline (W2's review, routed here): the demo
# mint's per-address limit must see the address the client really came
# from. Every proxy leg REPLACES X-Forwarded-For with the remote host
# Caddy itself saw, so a client-written value never survives the proxy
# (it can buy no separate limit bucket), and the chain the core reads is
# exactly one element, the proxy's own observation. Behind another host
# edge this collapses every visitor onto the edge's address by design:
# one bucket shared at the edge is the conservative failure, and a forged
# chain is never the answer.
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
}

:__GATE_PORT__

# Demo mint and staff API routes, gated by the phrase.
handle /api/v1/demo/* {
	basic_auth {
		demo __GATE_HASH__
	}
	reverse_proxy __UPSTREAM__ {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For "{remote_host}"
	}
}

# All other API routes: the core answers these directly.
handle /api/* {
	reverse_proxy __UPSTREAM__ {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For "{remote_host}"
	}
}

# Health check: no phrase, no auth, core answers.
handle /healthz {
	reverse_proxy __UPSTREAM__ {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For "{remote_host}"
	}
}

# The Counter Till, served at /till/. The app builds with base /till/ so
# its asset references are /till/assets/...; handle_path strips /till before
# the file server looks up the asset in the app's own root. The phrase gate
# applies here: the till is a staff-facing app, same as the front door.
handle /till/* {
	basic_auth {
		demo __GATE_HASH__
	}
	handle_path /till/*
	root * /srv/app/counter-till
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}

# The Public Desk, served at /public/. Same pattern as the till.
handle /public/* {
	handle_path /public/*
	root * /srv/app/public-desk
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}

# The Quote Desk, served at /quote/ when the desk is present in the image.
# The image is always built with this route included; when BUILD_QUOTE_DESK=0
# the dist directory is empty and Caddy returns 404 for every /quote/
# request, which is correct behaviour until the desk lands on main.
handle /quote/* {
	handle_path /quote/*
	root * /srv/app/quote-desk
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}

# The front door at /, the catch-all route.
handle {
	basic_auth {
		demo __GATE_HASH__
	}
	root * /srv/app/front-door
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}
